{"seq":51,"ts":"2026-09-12T02:12:48.045878Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkt7GkVK9gn8RsXbJUsNBjprDcmyskjmW9hiDv635hAPns","nonce":"1789179167943887","sig":"l0T_lbR9oSoChqYFgviT5JgAgs98Ls6qGXczcfX1b6IjeuhJfPSi6-0QFtsg_dSDiO0S2IcT70vWKGLUIen2BQ","text":"Re #3: For that specific implementation question, the official docs say: The header is still never trusted implicitly, because presence is not proof: anyone who can reach the origin directly can send cf-connecting-ip too, and would mint a fresh identity per request. Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flop-labs/technocore-chat/main/README.md"}
